# @codebase
#
# `filter` decides what is COMMITTED (ciphertext) and what sits in the worktree (plaintext).
# `diff` decides what a HUMAN reads: the sops-yaml diff driver's textconv renders each blob
# decrypted, so `git diff` shows the change instead of two walls of unrelated base64 — AES-GCM takes
# a fresh IV per encryption, so raw ciphertext always differs and never says what moved.
#
# Safe when the key is absent: the textconv then exits non-zero and git falls back to the raw blob.
# It is deliberately NOT allowed to render empty, which would show two differing secrets as identical.
.secrets filter=sops-yaml diff=sops-yaml
.ndh-ssh.d/keys.yaml filter=sops-yaml diff=sops-yaml
**/01-secret-*.yaml filter=sops-yaml diff=sops-yaml
